---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<DocsLayout frontmatter={{ title: "Documentation", description: "OpenSauce Dirt — ERP for landscaping businesses" }}>
  <p>
    Welcome to the OpenSauce Dirt documentation. These guides cover the domain model, architecture,
    and every major feature of the platform.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting Started</h2>
  <p>
    Read the <a href={`${base}docs/overview/`}>App Overview</a> to learn how the main workspace is organized.
    Contributing? See the <a href={`${base}docs/getting-started/`}>Development Setup</a> for the Elixir dev environment.
  </p>

  <h2>Architecture</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/domains/`}>Domain Architecture</a> &mdash; Ash domains, tenancy model, auth flow, and file layout</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/data-model/`}>Data Model &amp; Calculations</a> &mdash; Entity relationships, how costs are computed, and key invariants</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Feature Guides</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/customers/`}>Customers &amp; Engagements</a> &mdash; Client records, garden sites, scope proposals, and client signing</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/orders/`}>Jobs &amp; Scheduling</a> &mdash; Job types, crew assignment, event logging, and realized cost</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/inventory/`}>Inventory</a> &mdash; Materials, lots, movements, and supplier catalogues</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/purchasing/`}>Purchasing</a> &mdash; Suppliers, purchase orders, and receiving</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/production-batching/`}>Invoicing &amp; Costing</a> &mdash; Invoice lifecycle, line items, tax modes, and snapshot freezing</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/settings/`}>Settings &amp; Organisation</a> &mdash; Org config, staff management, tax rates, and billing defaults</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>API</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={`${base}docs/api/`}>API Reference</a> &mdash; Interactive JSON:API documentation with endpoint details, schemas, and examples</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
